menu "Board: Guition JC1060P470C_I_W_Y"

    choice BOARD_LCD_PANEL
        prompt "Default LCD panel variant"
        default BOARD_LCD_PANEL_NEW
        help
            The board ships with one of two glass panels behind the same JD9165 driver IC.
            They need different init tables and timing and cannot be detected at run time
            (docs/BOARD.md section 5). A "V2" label on the back means New.
            A wrong choice shows wrong colours or gamma, flickers, or stays black.

            This is only the default: the console command 'panel new|old' stores the
            choice in NVS, so both can be tried without rebuilding.

        config BOARD_LCD_PANEL_NEW
            bool "New panel (V2 label; factory firmware V3.7)"
        config BOARD_LCD_PANEL_OLD
            bool "Old panel (HKC QD070AS01-1; factory firmware V2.x)"
    endchoice

    config BOARD_LCD_DSI_LANE_MBPS
        int "MIPI-DSI lane bit rate (Mbps)"
        range 500 1500
        default 750
        help
            Every vendor source uses 750 Mbps except the xiaozhi "new" board (550).
            Its README suggests trying 550, 750 or 900 if the screen stays dark.

endmenu
